It seems like you are asking about how to implement comments in a programming language or project, but you haven't specified which one. Can you please provide more context or clarify which programming language or project you are referring to?

Assuming you want to know how to display comments in a Java-based GUI application, here's an example:

```java
import javax.swing.*;
import java.awt.*;

public class CommentsDisplay {
    private JFrame frame;
    private JTextArea textArea;

    public CommentsDisplay() {
        frame = new JFrame("Comments Display");
        frame.setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE);

        // Create a text area to display comments
        textArea = new JTextArea(10, 20);
        textArea.setEditable(false);

        // Add a button to add new comments
        JButton addButton = new JButton("Add Comment");
        addButton.addActionListener(e -> {
            String comment = JOptionPane.showInputDialog(frame, "Enter your comment:");
            if (comment != null) {
                textArea.append(comment + "\n");
            }
        });

        // Create a panel to hold the text area and button
        JPanel panel = new JPanel();
        panel.setLayout(new BorderLayout());
        panel.add(new JScrollPane(textArea), BorderLayout.CENTER);
        panel.add(addButton, BorderLayout.SOUTH);

        // Add the panel to the frame
        frame.getContentPane().add(panel);

        // Set the frame's size and make it visible
        frame.setSize(400, 300);
        frame.setVisible(true);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SwingUtilities.invokeLater(CommentsDisplay::new);
    }
}
```

This example creates a simple GUI application with a text area to display comments and a button to add new comments. When you click the "Add Comment" button, it opens an input dialog where you can enter your comment, which is then appended to the text area.

Please note that this is just a basic example, and you might need to adapt it to your specific requirements.
